The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': {'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': ['DISTRIBUTION_CENTERS', 'ORDERS', 'USERS', 'EVENTS', 'INVENTORY_ITEMS', 'PRODUCTS', 'ORDER_ITEMS']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
column name: potential usage  
• ORDER_ITEMS."created_at": timestamp of each item’s sale; use it to isolate rows that occurred in 2020 and to derive the calendar month.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": foreign‑key that links every sold item to PRODUCTS."id".  
• PRODUCTS."id": joins to ORDER_ITEMS."product_id".  
• PRODUCTS."name": human‑readable product name we ultimately want to show.  
• PRODUCTS."cost" & PRODUCTS."retail_price": needed to compute profit = retail_price – cost.  
• (optional) ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": can confirm that an item was actually sold, but profit is requested from PRODUCTS’ price & cost, so we focus on those.  
Conditions that may be used  
• YEAR( TO_TIMESTAMP( ORDER_ITEMS."created_at" / 1e6 ) ) = 2020 → restrict to 2020.  
• GROUP BY month expression (e.g. DATE_TRUNC('month', …)) when looking for the lowest profit each month.  
• HAVING MIN( profit ) to find the minimum per month.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (simple → complex → final) that look at the relevant columns, always limited to 20 rows for safety. Remember to replace the 1e6 divisor with 1000000 if you prefer integers.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Quick look at the PRODUCTS table: id, name, cost, retail_price, and computed profit.
SELECT 
  "id",
  "name",
  "cost",
  "retail_price",
  ("retail_price" - "cost") AS "profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Peek at ORDER_ITEMS to see raw timestamps and a couple of product links.
SELECT 
  "id",
  "product_id",
  "created_at",
  "sale_price"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show distinct calendar months present in ORDER_ITEMS for 2020.
SELECT DISTINCT
  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at" / 1000000)) AS "month_2020"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS"
WHERE YEAR( TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at" / 1000000) ) = 2020
ORDER BY "month_2020"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Combine ORDER_ITEMS with PRODUCTS to see profit for a handful of 2020 sales.
SELECT 
  oi."id" AS "order_item_id",
  p."name",
  p."cost",
  p."retail_price",
  (p."retail_price" - p."cost") AS "profit",
  TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000) AS "sold_ts"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE YEAR( TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000) ) = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Aggregate to find the minimum profit recorded for each calendar month of 2020.
SELECT
  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000)) AS "month",
  MIN(p."retail_price" - p."cost")                       AS "min_profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE YEAR( TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000) ) = 2020
GROUP BY "month"
ORDER BY "month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Return product names whose profit equals the minimum for January 2020 (as an example).
WITH jan AS (
  SELECT
    MIN(p."retail_price" - p."cost") AS "min_profit"
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
  JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
    ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
  WHERE DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000)) = '2020-01-01'
)
SELECT DISTINCT
  p."name",
  (p."retail_price" - p."cost") AS "profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
JOIN jan
  ON (p."retail_price" - p."cost") = jan."min_profit"
WHERE DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000)) = '2020-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Show lowest‑profit product(s) for every month of 2020, side‑by‑side.
WITH profits AS (
  SELECT
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000)) AS "month",
    p."name",
    (p."retail_price" - p."cost")                               AS "profit"
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
  JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
    ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
  WHERE YEAR( TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000) ) = 2020
)
SELECT
  pr."month",
  pr."name",
  pr."profit"
FROM profits pr
JOIN (
  SELECT
    "month",
    MIN("profit") AS "min_profit"
  FROM profits
  GROUP BY "month"
) mp
  ON pr."month" = mp."month"
 AND pr."profit" = mp."min_profit"
ORDER BY pr."month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Fuzzy search example—get any product names sold in 2020 containing ‘cap’.
SELECT DISTINCT
  p."name"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE YEAR( TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000) ) = 2020
  AND p."name" ILIKE '%cap%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: List distinct products that recorded sales in July 2020.
SELECT DISTINCT
  p."name"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000)) = '2020-07-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL—names of products that had sales in each month of 2020 and possessed the lowest profit for their respective month, ordered chronologically.
WITH monthly_profits AS (
  SELECT
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000)) AS "month",
    p."name",
    (p."retail_price" - p."cost")                               AS "profit"
  FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
  JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE."PRODUCTS"   p
    ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
  WHERE YEAR( TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at" / 1000000) ) = 2020
)
SELECT
  mp."month",
  mp."name",
  mp."profit"
FROM monthly_profits mp
JOIN (
  SELECT
    "month",
    MIN("profit") AS "min_profit"
  FROM monthly_profits
  GROUP BY "month"
) mins
  ON mp."month"  = mins."month"
 AND mp."profit" = mins."min_profit"
ORDER BY mp."month"
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is wrapped in double quotes for column names, uses only the permitted tables, and is limited to 20 records for safe exploration.
